  "question": {
    "text": "A long thin non-conducting cylindrical pipe of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;carrying a uniform surface charge density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>σ</mi></math>&nbsp;is rotating about its axis with a constant angular speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ω</mi></math>. The energy density of the magnetic field inside the tube is<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/9e9dabee-bb29-43a8-8827-21ddcb17c89e-image14.png\" />",
